  <p class="description">Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.</p>
  <p class="author-name">John Doe</p>
  <a href="https://example.com/post/123" class="link">Read more</a>
</div>
```

You can style this module using CSS to make it look the way you want. Here's an example of some basic styling:

```css
.post {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 20px;
}

.post img {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.categories {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}

.categories li {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-right: 10px;
}

.description {
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.author-name {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.link {
  display: inline-block;
  padding: 5px 10px;
  background-color: #4CAF50;
  color: white;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-radius: 5px;
}

.link:hover {
  background-color: #45a049;
}
```

Feel free to adjust the styles to fit your website's design.

